{
    "chapter_num": 18,
    "verses_count": 27,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Jethro’s Advice"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Jethro, the priest of Midian, Moses’ father-in-law, heard of all that God had done for Moses and for Israel His people—that the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " had brought Israel out of Egypt. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Jethro, Moses’ father-in-law, took Zipporah, Moses’ wife, after he had sent her back, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "with her two sons, of whom the name of one "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. Stranger There"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Gershom (for he said, “I have been a "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "sojourner, temporary resident"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "stranger in a foreign land”) "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and the name of the other "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. My God Is Help"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Eliezer (for "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "he said,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " “The God of my father "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " my help, and delivered me from the sword of Pharaoh”); "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and Jethro, Moses’ father-in-law, came with his sons and his wife to Moses in the wilderness, where he was encamped at the mountain of God. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now he had said to Moses, “I, your father-in-law Jethro, am coming to you with your wife and her two sons with her.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So Moses went out to meet his father-in-law, bowed down, and kissed him. And they asked each other about "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "their"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " well-being, and they went into the tent. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Moses told his father-in-law all that the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " had done to Pharaoh and to the Egyptians for Israel’s sake, all the hardship that had come upon them on the way, and "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "how"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " had delivered them. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Jethro rejoiced for all the good which the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " had done for Israel, whom He had delivered out of the hand of the Egyptians. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Jethro said, “Blessed "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "be"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": ", who has delivered you out of the hand of the Egyptians and out of the hand of Pharaoh, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "and"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " who has delivered the people from under the hand of the Egyptians. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now I know that the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " greater than all the gods; for in the very thing in which they "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "acted presumptuously"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "behaved proudly, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "He was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " above them.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Jethro, Moses’ father-in-law, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "So with MT, LXX; Syr., Tg., Vg. offered"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "took a burnt offering and "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "other"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " sacrifices "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "to offer"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " to God. And Aaron came with all the elders of Israel to eat bread with Moses’ father-in-law before God."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And so it was, on the next day, that Moses sat to judge the people; and the people stood before Moses from morning until evening. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So when Moses’ father-in-law saw all that he did for the people, he said, “What "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " this thing that you are doing for the people? Why do you alone "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Sit as judge"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "sit, and all the people stand before you from morning until evening?”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Moses said to his father-in-law, “Because the people come to me to inquire of God. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When they have a "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "dispute"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "difficulty, they come to me, and I judge between one and another; and I make known the statutes of God and His laws.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So Moses’ father-in-law said to him, “The thing that you do "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " not good. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Both you and these people who "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "are"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " with you will surely wear yourselves out. For this thing "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " too much for you; you are not able to perform it by yourself. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Listen now to my voice; I will give you "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "advice"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "counsel, and God will be with you: Stand before God for the people, so that you may bring the difficulties to God. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And you shall teach them the statutes and the laws, and show them the way in which they must walk and the work they must do. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Moreover you shall select from all the people able men, such as fear God, men of truth, hating covetousness; and place "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "such"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " over them "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "to be"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " rulers of thousands, rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And let them judge the people at all times. Then it will be "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "that"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " every great matter they shall bring to you, but every small matter they themselves shall judge. So it will be easier for you, for they will bear "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "the burden"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " with you. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 23,
                    "num_str": "23",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "If you do this thing, and God "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "so"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " commands you, then you will be able to endure, and all this people will also go to their place in peace.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 24,
                    "num_str": "24",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So Moses heeded the voice of his father-in-law and did all that he had said. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 25,
                    "num_str": "25",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Moses chose able men out of all Israel, and made them heads over the people: rulers of thousands, rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 26,
                    "num_str": "26",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So they judged the people at all times; the hard"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "difficult matters"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " cases they brought to Moses, but they judged every small case themselves."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 27,
                    "num_str": "27",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Moses let his father-in-law depart, and he went his way to his own land."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}